Scope of this license
---------------------

The MIT License set out below covers my original work in this repository: the
source code, the documentation, the figures, the notebook code, and the trained
model weights distributed as a release asset.

Two things are outside that grant.

1. The research manuscript, paper/Traffic_Sign_Robustness.pdf, is not covered
   by the MIT License. It remains my copyright and is published here for
   reading and citation.

2. The German Traffic Sign Recognition Benchmark (GTSRB), and material derived
   from its images, including the sign crops displayed as figures in
   notebooks/01_data_exploration.ipynb. GTSRB is the work of its authors and is
   governed by their terms. No ownership of the dataset is claimed here and no
   rights over it are granted. Anyone wishing to redistribute GTSRB images
   should obtain them from the dataset's authors and observe their terms.

The trained weights were produced by training on GTSRB. They are my own work
and are offered under the MIT License on that basis, which says nothing about,
and grants nothing over, the dataset they were trained on.

No third-party source code is vendored into this repository. Dependencies are
installed from their own distributions and are not redistributed here; each
remains under its own license.


